@startuml
title Xen RISC-V: APLIC MSI mode - routing IRQ 10 to domU1

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam BoxPadding 8

box "Host firmware / DT" #eeeeee
  participant "Host DT" as HDT
end box

box "Xen" #e8f0ff
  participant "boot / domain\nconstruction" as XBOOT
  participant "vintc" as VINTC
  participant "vaplic" as VAPLIC
  participant "aplic" as APLICC
end box

box "domU1 (dom0less)" #f0fff0
  participant "domU1 kernel\n(irq-riscv-aplic-msi.c)" as DOMU
end box

box "Hardware" #fff0f0
  participant "APLIC\n(S-level domain)" as APLIC
  participant "IMSIC\nhart 3, group 1" as IMSIC
  participant "UART" as UART
end box

note over HDT
  == Host DT (real hardware) ==
  imsics: interrupt-controller@28000000 {
      compatible = "riscv,imsics";
      reg = <0x0 0x28000000 0x0 0x1000000>,   // group 0
            <0x0 0x29000000 0x0 0x1000000>;   // group 1
      interrupt-controller;
      #interrupt-cells = <0>;
      msi-controller;
      riscv,num-ids = <255>;
      riscv,guest-index-bits  = <3>;   // LHXS = 3  -> 1 S file + 7 guest files per hart
      riscv,hart-index-bits   = <2>;   // LHXW = 2  -> 4 harts per group
      riscv,group-index-bits  = <1>;   // HHXW = 1  -> 2 groups
      riscv,group-index-shift = <24>;  // HHXS = group_index_shift - 24 = 0
      interrupts-extended = <&cpu0_intc 9>, ... , <&cpu7_intc 9>;
  };

  aplic_s: interrupt-controller@c000000 {
      compatible = "riscv,aplic";
      reg = <0x0 0x0c000000 0x0 0x8000>;
      interrupt-controller;
      #interrupt-cells = <2>;
      msi-parent = ~<&imsics>;           // => domaincfg.DM = 1
      riscv,num-sources = <96>;
  };

  serial@10000000 {
      compatible = "ns16550a";
      reg = <0x0 0x10000000 0x0 0x100>;
      interrupt-parent = ~<&aplic_s>;
      interrupts = <10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;   // <-- this is "IRQ 10"
  };

  == Host DT: dom0less domain description ==
  chosen {
      domU1 {
          compatible = "xen,domain";
          cpus = <2>;                      // vCPU0, vCPU1
          memory = <0x0 0x40000>;
          module@... { compatible = "multiboot,kernel", ...; };
          module@... { compatible = "multiboot,device-tree", ...; };
      };
  };

  == Partial DT passed as the "multiboot,device-tree" module ==
  /passthrough {
      serial@10000000 {
          compatible = "ns16550a";
          xen,path = "/soc/serial@10000000";
          xen,reg = <0x0 0x10000000 0x0 0x100 0x0 0x10000000>;
          interrupt-parent = ~<&aplic_s>;
          interrupts = <10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
      };
  };
end note

== Phase 0: boot, domU1 construction (once) ==

XBOOT -> HDT: parse /chosen/domU1 (compatible "xen,domain")\n2 vCPUs, kernel + partial-DT modules
XBOOT -> HDT: parse /passthrough/serial@10000000 from the partial DT
XBOOT -> XBOOT: map_device_irqs_to_domain(domU1, node)\nwalks "interrupts", skips IRQs of other INTCs
XBOOT -> XBOOT: map_irq_to_domain(domU1, irq=10, need_mapping=true, "serial")
XBOOT -> XBOOT: irq_permit_access(domU1, 10)\n(generic ownership rangeset, XSM/domctl)
XBOOT -> VINTC: vintc_reserve_virq(domU1, 10)\ntest_and_set_bit(10, used_irqs)
XBOOT -> XBOOT: route_irq_to_guest(domU1, virq=10, irq=10, "serial")

XBOOT -> XBOOT: make_intc_domU_node(): synthesise the APLIC + IMSIC\nnodes for domU1 at Xen-chosen guest addresses
XBOOT -> DOMU: hand over the fully generated guest DT
note over DOMU
  == Guest DT (generated by Xen for domU1) ==
  // Addresses are GUEST_* constants from asm/config.h. They are Xen's
  // choice and have nothing to do with the host layout above.
  imsics: interrupt-controller@GUEST_IMSIC_S_BASE {
      compatible = "riscv,imsics";
      reg = <... GUEST_IMSIC_S_BASE ... 0x2000>;   // one 4K page per vCPU
      interrupt-controller;
      #interrupt-cells = <0>;
      msi-controller;
      riscv,num-ids = <255>;
      interrupts-extended = <&vcpu0_intc 9>, <&vcpu1_intc 9>;
  };

  aplic: interrupt-controller@GUEST_APLIC_BASE {
      compatible = "riscv,aplic";
      reg = <... GUEST_APLIC_BASE ... 0x8000>;   // trapped by Xen, not real MMIO
      interrupt-controller;
      #interrupt-cells = <2>;
      msi-parent = ~<&imsics>;
      riscv,num-sources = <96>;      // guest_aplic_num_sources
  };

  serial@10000000 {
      compatible = "ns16550a";
      reg = <0x0 0x10000000 0x0 0x100>;   // per xen,reg, identity-mapped here
      interrupt-parent = ~<&aplic>;
      interrupts = <10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
  };
end note

== Phase 1: domU1 routes IRQ 10 to its vCPU1 (config time) ==

DOMU -> DOMU: request_irq() -> set_affinity picks vCPU1\ncompose MSI msg for its *virtual* IMSIC:\naddr = GUEST_IMSIC_S_BASE + 1*0x1000  (vCPU1's page)\n=> group=0, hart=1, guest=0
DOMU -> APLIC: writel(0x0004000A, GUEST_APLIC_BASE + 0x3000 + 10*4)\ntarget[10] = (hart_idx 1 << 18) | (guest 0 << 12) | EIID 10
note right of DOMU
  guest_index = 0 (harcoded in linux drivers/irqchip/irq-riscv-imsic-platform.c:79)
end note

APLIC --x VAPLIC: MMIO trap (GUEST_APLIC_BASE is not mapped)

VAPLIC -> VAPLIC: vaplic_emulate_store(curr, addr, 0x0004000A)\noffset falls in APLIC_TARGET_BASE...LAST\nsrcn = (offset - APLIC_GENMSI)/4 = 10
VAPLIC -> VINTC: AUTH_IRQ_BIT(domU1, 10)?
VINTC --> VAPLIC: true  (set in phase 0)

VAPLIC -> VAPLIC: hart_idx = value >> APLIC_TARGET_HART_IDX_SHIFT = 1\n=>\ntarget_vcpu = domain_vcpu(domU1, 1) = domU1->vcpu[1]
VAPLIC -> VAPLIC: domaincfg.DM == 1 (MSI mode)\nwrite_atomic(vaplic->regs.target[10], 0x0004000A)\n(guest's own value saved verbatim, see Phase 1b)
VAPLIC -> APLICC: aplic_msi_target_gen(target_vcpu, 0x0004000A)

APLICC -> APLICC: base_val &= APLIC_TARGET_EIID_MASK\n=> keeps only EIID 10; guest's Hart Index AND Guest Index discarded
APLICC -> APLICC: guest_id = vcpu_guest_file_id(vcpu1) = 1\n(which VS interrupt file on the physical hart belongs to this vCPU;\nselected by hstatus.VGEIN when the vCPU runs)
APLICC -> APLICC: hart_id = cpuid_to_hartid(vcpu1->processor) = 3\n(vCPU1 currently scheduled on Xen cpu 3)
APLICC -> APLICC: aplic_hart_field(3)
note right of APLICC
  lhxs = guest_index_bits = 3
  lhxw = hart_index_bits  = 2
  hhxw = group_index_bits = 1
  hhxs = group_index_shift - 24 = 0
  tppn = imsic->msi[cpu3].base_addr >> 12 = 0x29018000 >> 12 = 0x29018
  g    = (tppn >> (hhxs + 12)) & 1 = 0x29 & 1 = 1
  h    = (tppn >> lhxs) & 3 = 3
  return hart_index = (g << lhxw) | h = 7
end note
APLICC --> VAPLIC: (7 << 18) | (1 << 12) | 10 = 0x001C100A

VAPLIC -> APLIC: writel(0x001C100A, real aplic + 0x3028)

== Phase 1b: domU1 reads back target[10] (sanity check) ==

DOMU -> APLIC: readl(GUEST_APLIC_BASE + 0x3000 + 10*4)
APLIC --x VAPLIC: MMIO trap (GUEST_APLIC_BASE is not mapped)

VAPLIC -> VAPLIC: vaplic_emulate_load(curr, addr, out)\noffset falls in APLIC_TARGET_BASE...LAST
VAPLIC -> VINTC: AUTH_IRQ_BIT(domU1, 10)?
VINTC --> VAPLIC: true  (set in phase 0)
VAPLIC -> VAPLIC: vaplic_target_read(domU1, 10)\nreturns vaplic->regs.target[10]
note right of VAPLIC
  vaplic->regs.target[10] still holds the *guest's own*
  value 0x0004000A written in Phase 1 - vaplic_emulate_store()
  saved it before translating to the real hart_index/guest_index
  and writing 0x001C100A to hardware. The guest never sees the
  physical hart 3 / guest-file 1 encoding.
end note
VAPLIC --> APLIC: out = 0x0004000A
APLIC --> DOMU: 0x0004000A

== Phase 2: the interrupt actually fires (no software involved) ==

UART -> APLIC: level asserted on source 10
APLIC -> APLIC: read own target[10] = 0x001C100A\n Hart Index = 7 => g = 7 >> LHXW = 1 and h = 7 & 3 = 3\nguest_index = 1, EIID = 10
APLIC -> APLIC: build the MSI address from smsiaddrcfg / smsiaddrcfgh
note right of APLIC
  ppn = base_ppn | g << (HHXS + 12) | h << LHXS | guest_index
      = 0x29019

  MSI address = ppn << 12 = 0x29019000
end note
APLIC -> IMSIC: 4-byte write of data = 10 to 0x29019000 \n(= seteipnum_le of hart 3's guest interrupt file 1)
IMSIC -> IMSIC: set pending bit for identity 10\nin hart 3's guest interrupt file 1
IMSIC -> DOMU: vCPU1 resident (hstatus.VGEIN = 1) ->\nVS-level external interrupt taken directly
DOMU -> DOMU: handle UART, EOI in its own vIMSIC
@enduml
